# Mike Dabydeen GitHub Pages

Personal landing page built with Jekyll and hosted on GitHub Pages.

## Local development

```bash
bundle install
bundle exec jekyll serve
```

Local site: `http://127.0.0.1:4000`

## Build

```bash
bundle exec jekyll build
```

## GitHub Actions

- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: builds the Jekyll site on push/PR to catch template/content regressions.
- `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml`: builds and deploys to GitHub Pages on `main`.

To use action-based deployment, set repository Pages source to **GitHub Actions** in repository settings.

## Content structure

- `_posts/` for blog posts
- `_projects/` for open source highlights
- `_teaching/` for course resources
- `_data/` for profile and navigation data

## Contact setup

Contact options are configured in `_data/profile.yml`:

- `contact.issue_form_url`: link to the GitHub contact request form.
- `contact.form_endpoint`: optional external endpoint (for example Formspree) to enable the on-site contact form.
- `contact.email`: optional direct email address shown as a quick action.
